Z||000000||Philphine||11-14-2000||11:25 AM||||<BR>kind of intentional double post (also in mall section). i got a good deal on a gt rear facia but trying to get it shipped to me. ups and greyhound won't take it for size. the only way so far is truck freight, $138. i got a front facia via ups but the guy folded it in half and boxed it. surprised me but i got it ok (just unfolded it and set it in the sun). only cost about $25. any one tried to fold a rear facia or have any experience with shipping them? any body got a thrashed one they can fold to see what happens? any help or ideas appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-14-2000||02:39 PM||||You won't need to fold it in half....just fold the ends down.  Rear fascias are MUCH easier to ship than fronts.....just bend the ends over and tape them down.  Build a box for it that is within UPS specs and it will cost $15-$30 (depending on where you ship it and who is working). ||||reg||1
